10. REAL VOICE RECORDING AND QURAN RECITATION ASSESSMENT

This is a critical system that must be repaired completely.

Currently, recording and speech-to-text functionality have failed.

Implement a real recording and recognition pipeline.

A. Microphone recording

- Request microphone permissions.
- Verify microphone availability.
- Start recording.
- Pause and resume where supported.
- Stop recording.
- Display recording status.
- Display recording duration.
- Save audio files.
- Play back recordings.
- Delete or retry recordings.
- Handle permission denial.
- Handle interruptions.
- Handle recording errors.

Never display a recording indicator unless actual audio is being captured.

B. Arabic speech-to-text

When I recite the Quran, NOOR must listen to my voice and convert it into written Arabic text.

Expected workflow:

1. Select Surah and Ayah range.
2. Press Start Recording.
3. Recite the Quran.
4. Capture the actual microphone audio.
5. Process the recording.
6. Convert the recitation into Arabic text.
7. Display the recognized words in the application.
8. Compare the recognized text against verified Quran text.
9. Display possible mistakes.

Use a suitable Arabic speech recognition engine, preferably specialized Quranic recognition.

Support offline recognition where a suitable model is available.

Do not require paid external APIs.

Do not return an empty transcript silently.

If recognition fails, explain why.

C. Recitation assessment

Detect possible:

- Omitted words.
- Added words.
- Replaced words.
- Repeated words.
- Skipped Ayahs.
- Incorrect verse order.
- Long pauses.

Display:

- Correct words.
- Words requiring review.
- Suspected mistakes.
- Current Surah.
- Current Ayah.
- Overall assessment.

Distinguish between actual textual errors and speech-recognition uncertainty.

Do not classify pronunciation differences as definite mistakes without reliable evidence.

Allow teachers to review and approve assessments.

D. Two separate audio modes

Listen and Follow

The application plays Sheikh audio and highlights the corresponding Ayahs.

My Recitation and Memorization

The application records the user's voice, converts it into Arabic text, compares it with the Quran, and evaluates the result.

These modes must not interfere with each other.

